                             <item>
                              <widget class="QGroupBox" name="group_algoH2Datum">
                               <property name="title">
                                <string/>
                               </property>
                               <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="vl_algoH2Datum">
                                <item>
                                 <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="hl_algoH2DatumHdr">
                                  <item>
                                   <widget class="QRadioButton" name="radio_algoH2Datum">
                                    <property name="font">
                                     <font>
                                      <pointsize>10</pointsize>
                                      <weight>75</weight>
                                      <bold>true</bold>
                                     </font>
                                    </property>
                                    <property name="toolTip">
                                     <string>Fits the reference plane that every height in section 3 is measured FROM. Get this wrong and nothing downstream can be recovered.

Place the ROIs on the substrate and spread them as widely as possible. Corners constrain tilt far better than the middle - each ROI already contributes thousands of pixels, so what is scarce is lever arm, not data.

Three ROIs define a plane exactly, with no redundancy and no error estimate. Four or more make it overdetermined, which averages the noise down and produces the RMS residual this section gates on.

Selecting this section shows the straightened part view and its datum ROIs.</string>
                                    </property>
                                    <property name="styleSheet">
                                     <string notr="true">color: rgb(255, 255, 255);</string>
                                    </property>
                                    <property name="text">
                                     <string>2 - Fit Datum Plane</string>
                                    </property>
                                    <attribute name="buttonGroup">
                                     <string notr="true">buttonGroup_algoH2Section</string>
                                    </attribute>
                                   </widget>
                                  </item>
                                  <item>
                                   <widget class="QToolButton" name="toolButton_algoH2RunDatum">
                                    <property name="enabled">
                                     <bool>false</bool>
                                    </property>
                                    <property name="minimumSize">
                                     <size>
                                      <width>34</width>
                                      <height>26</height>
                                     </size>
                                    </property>
                                    <property name="toolTip">
                                     <string>Fit the plane on its own.

Needs stage 1 to have passed - the ROIs are placed relative to the part pose, so without it there is nothing to place them against. Re-running this clears stage 3, whose heights are all measured from this plane.</string>
                                    </property>
                                    <property name="text">
                                     <string/>
                                    </property>
                                    <property name="icon">
                                     <iconset resource="VisionApp.qrc">
                                      <normaloff>:/24x24/Icon/24x24/cil-media-play.png</normaloff>:/24x24/Icon/24x24/cil-media-play.png</iconset>
                                    </property>
