                                    <property name="toolTip">
                                     <string>Only pixels whose raw grey value falls in this range are used for the fit. This is the filter that keeps dropouts (grey 0) and interpolation artefacts out of the datum - on a real production scan about 3% of pixels hold heights the sensor physically cannot measure, and they have normal-looking intensity, so nothing else catches them.</string>
